WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.333
<i>Fluttering and dancing in the sky</i>

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:17.708
<i>Let our love reach you...</i>

00:00:17.708 --> 00:00:18.458
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:00:18.458 --> 00:00:19.542
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:20.958
<i>LOVE...</i>

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.000
<i>ohhhh... SAY!</i>

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.417
<i>This heart</i>

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:28.708
<i>Try and move it</i>

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:31.833
<i>Look, how should I show you?</i>

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.000
<i>Then together with us</i>

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.375
<i>Let's dance! Take my hand</i>

00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:35.833
<i>hey yeah yeah!</i>

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:37.333
<i>Leave it to me</i>

00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:40.250
<i>to escort you! ALL RIGHT!</i>

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.958
<i>As if worrying, the passing rain</i>

00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:46.417
<i>caressed my cheek gently,</i>
<i>so as not to be noticed.</i>

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:50.375
<i>Jumping over faster than a shooting star</i>

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:53.833
<i>Reach out your hand!</i>

00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:54.750
<i>let's get LOVE!</i>

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.375
<i>Shout to the moon! (shout!)</i>

00:00:56.375 --> 00:00:58.000
<i>Let your shout ring out! (shout!)</i>

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.167
<i>What's up, what's up?</i>

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.917
<i>Let me hear your voice</i>

00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:02.458
<i>Undo your hair</i>

00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:05.458
<i>Saying goodbye to yesterday</i>

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:06.458
<i>when my eyes were closed</i>

00:01:06.458 --> 00:01:09.000
<i>A single petal fluttering lightly</i>

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.875
<i>Spit it out, SHOUT! (shout!)</i>

00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:12.708
<i>Shout out your feelings! (shout!)</i>

00:01:12.708 --> 00:01:13.458
<i>Isn't it fine</i>

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:15.583
<i>if nothing is for sure?</i>

00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:16.625
<i>wow yeah!</i>

00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:17.125
<i>That's right</i>

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:18.958
<i>Let's put away the lies</i>

00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:21.667
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.583
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.750
"Round Moon"

00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:50.667
Please support us!

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:53.333
Cut! Okay!

00:01:53.333 --> 00:01:55.333
Thank you very much!

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:01.667
That was fun!

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:05.333
You're lucky, Kurisu.
You weren't even nervous on TV.

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:07.167
Of course not!

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:11.875
I am a perfect genius!
The golden beauty, the great Kurisu Hijiri!

00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:14.958
Why should <i>I </i>be nervous?

00:02:16.875 --> 00:02:20.333
Oh, Kurisu's on a roll today, too!

00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:24.500
Acting the part of a charming fool
is her specialty, Reina.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.625
Ah, your sharp tongue is on a roll, too, Tsubaki.

00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:30.667
Oh my.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:33.792
Hello, dear princesses.

00:02:34.708 --> 00:02:37.833
Shun, Rui, good work today.

00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:40.000
We're not princesses! We're godde--

00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:44.458
How do you do, Shun?

00:02:44.458 --> 00:02:49.125
The Hajime fan gathering the other day
was very worthwhile, wasn't it?

00:02:49.125 --> 00:02:54.875
Yes, it was a lovely tea party with a gathering
of the best of those in Hajime's fan club.

00:02:54.875 --> 00:02:56.750
We must do it again.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.917
Yes, I would gladly participate.

00:03:00.917 --> 00:03:03.708
Speaking of which, are the others around?

00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:06.625
Oh, the others have left early
to return to the moo--

00:03:06.625 --> 00:03:09.542
She means, they returned to the dorm!

00:03:10.417 --> 00:03:12.708
Shun, it's about time.

00:03:12.708 --> 00:03:14.542
You're right.

00:03:14.542 --> 00:03:18.542
Then, until next time, dear goddesses.

00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:30.125
Our conversation yesterday
was quite thrilling, was it not?

00:03:30.125 --> 00:03:34.958
Jeez! I was so surprised!
Kurisucchi said "goddess" and everything!

00:03:34.958 --> 00:03:36.792
B-But that's...

00:03:36.792 --> 00:03:38.208
Be careful.

00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:41.958
The people of Earth must not find out

00:03:41.958 --> 00:03:46.125
that we are inhabitants of the moon.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:50.958
The twelve of us gather the feelings
of the people of the Earth

00:03:50.958 --> 00:03:54.833
in order to become the beings whoĀ
stability to both the moon and the Earth--

00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:58.292
moon goddesses, what we aim to
become as goddess candidates.

00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:03.292
I'll bet the people on Earth would
never guess that we'd come here as idols

00:04:03.292 --> 00:04:06.375
as part of our goddess training.

00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:15.917
Oh, the demon king is drinking tea again.

00:04:15.917 --> 00:04:17.542
You're right.

00:04:17.542 --> 00:04:20.625
He's always unnecessarily elegant.

00:04:20.625 --> 00:04:24.042
You two, if you're going to spy on someone,
then spy on the great Hajime.

00:04:24.042 --> 00:04:25.458
That's what you have a problem with?

00:04:25.458 --> 00:04:28.667
Um, guys? If you spy on others
with the transporter,

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.667
we'll get in trouble again.

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:33.917
You look like you're having fun, little ones.

00:04:33.917 --> 00:04:35.000
Hey.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.375
How do you do?

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:40.917
Tsubaki and Reina, you two also came
to visit this dorm after all, huh?

00:04:40.917 --> 00:04:42.000
Guys!

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.292
What are you all doing here?

00:04:44.292 --> 00:04:48.625
Matsuri said she wanted to show
everyone her new invention.

00:04:48.625 --> 00:04:50.000
So--

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.000
I made something wonderful again.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.667
I call it the "Increase Femininity by 100% Gun!"

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:59.458
By slightly altering the structure of one's DNA,

00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:02.167
it can exponentially increase
one's feminine charms.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.917
As long as we have this,
we'll definitely have a surge of fans!

00:05:04.917 --> 00:05:06.708
DNA structure...

00:05:06.708 --> 00:05:08.208
...alterations?

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:12.750
K-Kurisu?

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.250
What a coincidence, Matsuri.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.542
I also just happened to complete my invention.

00:05:17.542 --> 00:05:21.167
If you drink some, you'll be
the owner of a sexy body in no time.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:24.875
I call it "Adult Woman Go-Go Poison!"

00:05:24.875 --> 00:05:26.292
Poison?!

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:29.542
From the name, I already have
an extremely bad feeling about it.

00:05:29.542 --> 00:05:30.958
This is perfect!

00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:33.875
Mad Scientist Matsuri Motomiya!

00:05:33.875 --> 00:05:37.875
I have always wanted a direct match with you.

00:05:37.875 --> 00:05:43.167
See the invention of the great
genius Kurisu in person and weep!

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:47.667
Because <i>my </i>invention will <i>definitely</i>
be more effective than <i>your</i>s!

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:52.250
Hina, I appoint you as
glorious test subject No. 1!

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.542
Be grateful!

00:05:53.542 --> 00:05:54.750
What?!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:06:00.208
Wait. As a scientist, I accept
any challenge thrust before me.

00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:04.458
So, Hina, take a shot from my gun first.

00:06:04.458 --> 00:06:05.875
I won't let you!

00:06:05.875 --> 00:06:07.583
What...?!

00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:13.750
What is all the fuss about?

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.542
Is everyone all right?

00:06:17.333 --> 00:06:19.792
A fire? Or an illusion?

00:06:19.792 --> 00:06:21.125
Oh no!

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.083
Whoa, what's this?!

00:06:52.542 --> 00:06:54.250
Hm? Huh?

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:55.875
What?!

00:06:55.875 --> 00:06:59.292
W-We've... become Tsukiusa bunnies...

00:06:59.292 --> 00:07:01.167
What is the meaning of this?

00:07:01.167 --> 00:07:03.125
U-Um...

00:07:03.125 --> 00:07:04.875
Oh my, oh my.

00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:09.750
It appears the powers of the two inventions
caused a strange chemical reaction.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:12.917
P-Please be more disturbed by this, Mizuki!

00:07:12.917 --> 00:07:14.083
Kurisu.

00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:15.458
Kurisu...

00:07:15.458 --> 00:07:17.417
How many times do I have to tell you

00:07:17.417 --> 00:07:20.792
not to use experimental inventions that
haven't been tested for safety in the dorms!

00:07:20.792 --> 00:07:22.375
I can't believe this child!

00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:24.625
I-It's not <i>my </i>fault!

00:07:24.625 --> 00:07:28.375
This is... an unfortunate coincidence,
I mean, an accident...

00:07:28.375 --> 00:07:33.667
It's clear what caused this, so we should
be able to return to normal... right?

00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:35.917
No problemo. There is a way.

00:07:35.917 --> 00:07:40.292
I thought this might happen,
so I built a reset function into the gun.

00:07:42.292 --> 00:07:47.750
However, the light crystal
needed to shoot the reset beam

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.583
was lost in the explosion earlier.

00:07:50.583 --> 00:07:53.917
With just this, we cannot return to normal.

00:07:53.917 --> 00:07:55.792
H-Hina, get a hold of yourself!

00:07:55.792 --> 00:08:00.250
Oh no! I didn't think about what
my future would be like as a Tsukiusa bunny.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.583
Most people wouldn't.

00:08:02.583 --> 00:08:05.833
Matsuri, you do not have spare light crystals?

00:08:05.833 --> 00:08:07.583
Unfortunately, no.

00:08:07.583 --> 00:08:12.125
However, if you give me two or
three days, I can make new ones.

00:08:12.125 --> 00:08:15.542
It can't be helped.
Then for just two or three days...

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:19.083
What's the matter, Kurisu?

00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:25.667
My invention, "Adult Woman Go-Go
Poison," has an adhesive ingredient

00:08:25.667 --> 00:08:27.625
to make sure the transformation sticks.

00:08:27.625 --> 00:08:31.625
If we stay in this form for too long...

00:08:31.625 --> 00:08:35.542
...we may not be able to
completely return to our old forms...

00:08:39.167 --> 00:08:41.042
What...?!

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:47.958
Excuse us...

00:08:47.958 --> 00:08:49.000
It's quiet...

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.292
I wonder if anyone's here...

00:08:51.292 --> 00:08:55.500
At this time of day,
it's possible everyone's out working.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:56.917
That would be convenient.

00:08:56.917 --> 00:09:01.875
Matsuri, are you sure that light crystal
flew into Procella's dorms?

00:09:01.875 --> 00:09:05.667
There is no mistake. I followed
it with the transporter, spyi--

00:09:05.667 --> 00:09:07.875
--watching over it.

00:09:09.958 --> 00:09:12.000
<i>Watching over it.</i>

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.917
She's insisting on it!

00:09:13.917 --> 00:09:17.458
Let's leave questions about that till later.

00:09:17.458 --> 00:09:21.750
So, how many do we need in order
to shoot the resetting beam?

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:23.667
You pretty much need one per person.

00:09:23.667 --> 00:09:25.583
That many?

00:09:25.583 --> 00:09:27.667
The dorm curfew is 8 p.m.

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:29.875
We must return before that.

00:09:29.875 --> 00:09:32.208
We don't have much time.

00:09:32.208 --> 00:09:36.417
Everyone, let's split up and look
for the light crystals, quickly!

00:09:36.417 --> 00:09:39.083
We must return to our
original forms before the day is out!

00:09:39.083 --> 00:09:40.500
Yeah!

00:09:46.708 --> 00:09:48.292
Here's one!

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:52.625
Got it!

00:09:57.375 --> 00:09:59.667
Just one more! Let's do our best!

00:09:59.667 --> 00:10:01.000
Yeah!

00:10:12.625 --> 00:10:14.917
Nothing! I don't see anything!

00:10:14.917 --> 00:10:16.292
Just one more...

00:10:16.292 --> 00:10:18.042
Where could it be?

00:10:19.833 --> 00:10:21.708
Kai, are you back?

00:10:22.875 --> 00:10:24.375
Ruicchi was home?

00:10:24.375 --> 00:10:27.042
Oh dear. I did not notice at all.

00:10:27.042 --> 00:10:28.625
Wh-Wh-Wh-What should we do?

00:10:28.625 --> 00:10:31.042
We just have to get through this!

00:10:31.042 --> 00:10:32.458
Kai?

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:35.708
Huh?

00:10:37.083 --> 00:10:39.333
A Tsukiusa bunny in a place like this?

00:10:45.167 --> 00:10:49.042
Did Kai always have this many Tsukiusas out?

00:10:49.042 --> 00:10:51.208
Maybe Shun put up more...

00:10:51.208 --> 00:10:52.625
Oh well.

00:10:54.542 --> 00:10:56.625
Th-Th-That was close!

00:11:00.875 --> 00:11:03.833
Rui, you'll be home by yourself tomorrow, right?

00:11:03.833 --> 00:11:06.750
I made pudding, so have it as a snack.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.250
Okay.

00:11:12.333 --> 00:11:13.708
Pudding...

00:11:15.208 --> 00:11:17.583
What's the matter, Hina? Hurry up and get go--

00:11:17.583 --> 00:11:19.000
--ing.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:19.792
Oh my.

00:11:19.792 --> 00:11:22.125
Stare...

00:11:25.333 --> 00:11:28.708
Wh-What do we do?!

00:11:37.417 --> 00:11:39.417
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What should we do?!

00:11:39.417 --> 00:11:42.500
We have no choice.
Now that he knows our secret--

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.333
We have no choice but to do it.

00:11:46.083 --> 00:11:48.250
Hinachin, it was a joke.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:51.458
Anyway, we just need to get
through this somehow...

00:11:51.458 --> 00:11:53.417
Are you all Tsukiusas?

00:11:53.417 --> 00:11:55.292
Why can you move?

00:11:55.292 --> 00:11:58.375
Is he just accepting this normally?

00:11:58.375 --> 00:12:00.917
Are you special bunnies made by Shun?

00:12:00.917 --> 00:12:06.208
Oh, yes, yes! He really can do anything!
The demon king's amazing!

00:12:06.208 --> 00:12:08.083
What were you doing earlier?

00:12:08.083 --> 00:12:09.500
Looking for something?

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.042
U-Um...

00:12:11.042 --> 00:12:13.333
It appears he does not know who we really are.

00:12:13.333 --> 00:12:16.500
Why don't we try explaining the circumstances
to him without giving away too much?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.125
But it looks like he can't understand what we're saying.

00:12:20.125 --> 00:12:23.375
Then we'll tell him with
gestures or whatever we need to!

00:12:23.375 --> 00:12:24.875
Go, Hina!

00:12:30.833 --> 00:12:35.083
"We"...? "Came from"... "the sky"...?

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:40.333
"That stone is"...

00:12:43.375 --> 00:12:44.792
...what you're looking for?

00:12:50.042 --> 00:12:51.458
"Yoru"?

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.208
"English-Japanese Dictionary"

00:12:55.333 --> 00:12:57.750
In English? "Night"?

00:13:01.917 --> 00:13:03.417
"Dead"?

00:13:06.333 --> 00:13:07.750
"Round"?

00:13:10.542 --> 00:13:12.042
You're dead if you don't look
around and find it by nightfall?

00:13:15.042 --> 00:13:16.625
Then, do you want me to help?

00:13:17.708 --> 00:13:19.958
I'll help you find that stone.

00:13:21.958 --> 00:13:26.708
Actually, I think Shun had
something like that this morning...

00:13:27.958 --> 00:13:29.208
What?!

00:13:32.167 --> 00:13:33.708
This is Shun's room.

00:13:33.708 --> 00:13:35.583
What?

00:13:35.583 --> 00:13:37.000
Okay, let's go in.

00:13:43.875 --> 00:13:45.583
What's going on?

00:13:45.583 --> 00:13:47.625
An unexpected development!

00:13:47.625 --> 00:13:50.583
What the heck? Why is this
the only room that's so big?

00:13:50.583 --> 00:13:52.625
It's obvious something strange is going on!

00:13:52.625 --> 00:13:54.500
Is it a doorway to another dimension?

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.583
No one thinks this is strange?!

00:14:00.792 --> 00:14:02.375
That's Shun for you.

00:14:02.375 --> 00:14:04.167
He's good.

00:14:04.167 --> 00:14:05.583
Well, let's look around.

00:14:11.125 --> 00:14:13.125
Let's see...

00:14:13.125 --> 00:14:15.167
Let's see.

00:14:15.167 --> 00:14:17.125
Let's see!

00:14:17.125 --> 00:14:18.542
Let's see.

00:14:23.333 --> 00:14:24.750
There was nothing there, huh?

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.958
I wonder where he put it...

00:14:26.958 --> 00:14:29.500
Let's take a break and then look again.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:31.208
I'll get some drinks.

00:14:36.417 --> 00:14:39.583
This is the live TV show Shun is on right now.

00:14:45.208 --> 00:14:47.417
Shun took it with him?

00:14:47.417 --> 00:14:50.208
I can ask him for it when he comes home...

00:14:52.375 --> 00:14:54.625
...but he's not coming home tonight.

00:14:56.417 --> 00:15:00.958
After this live broadcast, he said he would
be going straight out of town on location.

00:15:00.958 --> 00:15:02.833
He won't be back until tomorrow.

00:15:03.833 --> 00:15:07.667
Tomorrow? Then we won't be able
to return to normal today!

00:15:07.667 --> 00:15:09.333
What should we do?

00:15:18.333 --> 00:15:19.750
It's over...

00:15:21.708 --> 00:15:23.958
"Mr. Shun Shimotsuki"

00:15:24.625 --> 00:15:26.042
Shun?

00:15:28.458 --> 00:15:29.958
Um, excuse me.

00:15:29.958 --> 00:15:32.042
Huh? Mr. Minaduki?

00:15:32.042 --> 00:15:33.667
Um, where's Shun?

00:15:33.667 --> 00:15:39.375
M-Mr. Shimotsuki changed and left
right after the live broadcast...

00:15:42.583 --> 00:15:45.708
He should still have some time...

00:15:45.708 --> 00:15:48.167
Did he already leave for the station?

00:15:48.167 --> 00:15:51.833
Then, even if we went after Shun now...

00:15:51.833 --> 00:15:53.083
Hina...

00:15:53.083 --> 00:15:57.417
S-Stupid Hina! Stop bawling like that!

00:15:57.417 --> 00:15:59.750
Are you going to just give up?!

00:16:00.292 --> 00:16:03.875
We've been working hard
all this time to become goddesses!

00:16:03.875 --> 00:16:08.667
We... We can't give up just
because of something like this!

00:16:08.667 --> 00:16:11.583
My determination isn't something
to be taken so lightly!

00:16:11.583 --> 00:16:17.125
Even if I remain a bunny, I'll still
show everyone I can become a goddess!

00:16:17.125 --> 00:16:18.917
Kurisu...

00:16:18.917 --> 00:16:21.083
Don't cry.

00:16:21.083 --> 00:16:25.000
You know what? I have a goal and a dream, too.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.875
There are times when I can't
move forward like I want to.

00:16:27.875 --> 00:16:30.250
And times when I mess up.

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:33.875
But I don't want to give up,
so I'll work hard until the end.

00:16:33.875 --> 00:16:35.583
That's what I've decided.

00:16:35.583 --> 00:16:38.042
Because I'm an idol.

00:16:38.042 --> 00:16:41.917
I heard that idols cheer everyone on.

00:16:41.917 --> 00:16:47.375
So if I give up, then I can't cheer on my fans.

00:16:47.375 --> 00:16:50.458
That's why I won't give up.

00:16:50.458 --> 00:16:53.458
I'll definitely help you guys, too.

00:16:53.458 --> 00:16:58.000
He's right. You can't give up, Kurisu!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.250
Of course not.

00:17:00.333 --> 00:17:02.042
That's right! We can't give up!

00:17:02.042 --> 00:17:06.542
Even if this doesn't work, there are things
like cat-shaped robots in this world!

00:17:06.542 --> 00:17:10.667
Rabbit-shaped goddesses are like
mascot characters! People would love them!

00:17:10.667 --> 00:17:12.667
To give up after a small setback like this

00:17:12.667 --> 00:17:16.167
means you're not qualified
to be an idol, let alone a goddess!

00:17:16.167 --> 00:17:19.333
You have to learn from the
protagonists of sports comics!

00:17:19.333 --> 00:17:22.083
All right! I'm fired up now!

00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:24.167
Reina, that's stifling.

00:17:24.167 --> 00:17:27.625
Now that that's decided,
let's go after Shun, everyone!

00:17:27.625 --> 00:17:29.250
Hina, tell Rui.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.958
What? Again?

00:17:30.958 --> 00:17:32.917
I-I mean I'll do it, but...

00:17:34.042 --> 00:17:34.792
Wait.

00:17:34.792 --> 00:17:35.750
Huh?

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:37.625
What's the matter, Tsubaki?

